#subtitle: Issues of taxation, budget, and tariffs.

= Fiscal Policy

Fiscal policy involves issues of taxation and budget.


@fiscal_menu

Upper-income tax rates: [+ upper_tax_rates : taxation +]

Lower-income tax rates: [+ lower_tax_rates : taxation +]

- @raise_rich: Increase taxes on the rich.
- @raise_poor
- @raise_overall: Increase overall taxes.
- @cut_rich
- @cut_poor
- @cut_overall: Cut overall taxes.
- @raise_progressive: Make the tax system more progressive by raising taxes on the rich and cutting them for the poor.
- @regressive
- @tariffs
- @root: Do not change the tax system.
- @easy_discard
- @cancel_advisor_action

@raise_progressive
subtitle: This does not change overall revenue. [? if lower_tax_rates < -5 : Lower-class tax rates are too low to cut anymore. ?] [? if upper_tax_rates > 5 : Upper-class tax rates are too high to increase. ?]
choose-if: lower_tax_rates >= -5 and upper_tax_rates <= 5 and econ_moderation < 8
on-arrival: urban_linke += ((7+issue_cost_of_living)/3)*(1-dissent); upper_linke -= 2; rural_linke -= 1; upper_tax_rates += 1; lower_tax_rates -= 1; capital_strike_progress += 1; capital_strike_progress += 1 if upper_tax_rates > 1; capital_strike_progress += 1 if upper_tax_rates > 3; upper_spd -= 2 if upper_tax_rates > 1; greens_relation -= 1; spd_relation -= 1; upper_greens -= 3 if (in_rrgreen_coalition == 1); upper_spd -= 3 if (in_rrgreen_coalition == 1); fdp_relation -= 2; cdu_relation -= 2; upper_fdp += 1; issue_cost_of_living -= 0.5; 

@raise_rich
subtitle: +2 budget
unavailable-subtitle: Tax rates are already too high. or econ moderation
choose-if: upper_tax_rates <= 5 and econ_moderation < 8
on-arrival: upper_tax_rates += 1; capital_strike_progress += 1; capital_strike_progress += 1 if upper_tax_rates > 1; capital_strike_progress += 1 if upper_tax_rates > 3; urban_linke += 3*(1-dissent); upper_linke -= 4; rural_linke -= 1; upper_greens -= 3 if (in_rrgreen_coalition == 1); upper_spd -= 3 if (in_rrgreen_coalition == 1); budget += 2; unemployed += 1; inflation -= 0.6; economic_growth -= 0.4; fdp_relation -= 2; cdu_relation -= 2; upper_fdp += 1;

@raise_poor
title: Raise consumption taxes, which disproportionately affect the poor.
subtitle: +2 budget
unavailable-subtitle: Tax rates are already too high. or econ moderation
choose-if: lower_tax_rates <= 5 and econ_moderation >= 4
on-arrival: budget += 2; urban_linke -= 4; east_linke -= 4; rural_linke -= 2; youth_linke -= 2; lower_tax_rates += 1; urban_linke -= 4 if lower_tax_rates >= 2; oldleft_dissent += 6; beweli_dissent += 6; emali_dissent += 6; pragmatist_dissent += 3; econ_moderation += 1; upper_linke += 1*(1-dissent); cdu_relation += 5*(1-dissent); fdp_relation += 5*(1-dissent); urban_greens -= 3 if (in_rrgreen_coalition == 1); urban_spd -= 3 if (in_rrgreen_coalition == 1); greens_coalition_dissent += 1; spd_coalition_dissent += 0.7;

We have raised taxes for the poor and working class. This hurts our support among the workers.

@cut_overall
subtitle: -3 budget
unavailable-subtitle: -3 budget - [? if upper_tax_rates < -5 or lower_tax_rates < -5 : Tax rates are already too low. ?]
choose-if: budget >= 3 and upper_tax_rates >= -5 and lower_tax_rates >= -5
on-arrival: budget -= 3; upper_tax_rates -= 1; lower_tax_rates -= 1; youth_linke += 5*(1-dissent); upper_linke += 4*(1-dissent); urban_linke += 3*(1-dissent); econ_moderation += 1; upper_greens += 3*(1-dissent) if (in_rrgreen_coalition == 1); upper_spd += 3*(1-dissent) if (in_rrgreen_coalition == 1); cdu_relation += 5; fdp_relation += 5; unemployed -= 1.5 if unemployed >= 5; capital_strike_progress -= 1 if upper_tax_rates < 0; inflation += 1; economic_growth += 0.6; 

@cut_poor
title: Cut consumption taxes for the poor.
subtitle: -2 budget
unavailable-subtitle: -2 budget - [? if lower_tax_rates < -5: Tax rates are already too low. ?]
choose-if: budget >= 2 and lower_tax_rates >= -5
on-arrival: budget -= 2; lower_tax_rates -= 1; urban_linke += ((7+issue_cost_of_living)/3)*(1-dissent); unemployed -= 0.7 if unemployed >= 5; inflation += 0.6; economic_growth += 0.4; issue_cost_of_living -= 0.5; 

Our tax cuts disproportionately benefit the poor and working class.

@cut_rich
title: Cut income taxes for the rich.
subtitle: -2 budget
unavailable-subtitle: -2 budget - [? if upper_tax_rates < -5: Tax rates are already too low. ?]
choose-if: budget >= 2 and upper_tax_rates >= -5 and econ_moderation >= 6
on-arrival: budget -= 2; upper_tax_rates -= 1; upper_linke += 5*(1-dissent); rural_linke += 3*(1-dissent); upper_greens += 3*(1-dissent) if greens_in_government; upper_spd += 3*(1-dissent) if spd_in_government; upper_fdp -= 1; fdp_relation += 5*(1-dissent); cdu_relation += 5*(1-dissent); unemployed -= 0.7 if unemployed >= 5; capital_strike_progress -= 1 if upper_tax_rates < 0; inflation += 0.6; economic_growth += 0.4; oldleft_dissent += 10; beweli_dissent += 10; emali_dissent += 7; pragmatist_dissent += 3; econ_moderation += 1; greens_coalition_dissent += 1; spd_coalition_dissent += 0.7;

We have reduced income and property taxes for the rich and middle class. The bourgeois parties approve of this orthodox economic course.

@raise_overall
subtitle: +3 budget
unavailable-subtitle: Tax rates are already too high.
choose-if: upper_tax_rates <= 5 and lower_tax_rates <= 5
on-arrival: budget += 3; urban_linke -= 4; rural_linke -= 2; youth_linke -= 4; east_linke -= 4; urban_greens -= 2 if greens_in_government; urban_spd -= 2 if spd_in_government; urban_fdp += 1; upper_fdp += 1; spd_relation -= 1; greens_relation -= 1; cdu_relation -= 2; fdp_relation -= 2; unemployed += 2; lower_tax_rates += 1; upper_tax_rates += 1; capital_strike_progress += 1 if upper_tax_rates > 1; capital_strike_progress += 1 if upper_tax_rates > 2; urban_linke -= 2 if lower_tax_rates > 1; inflation -= 1.1; economic_growth -= 0.6; upper_linke -= 1; beweli_dissent += 2; emali_dissent += 2;

Raising taxes hurts our support among all those who pay taxes. [? if in_grand_coalition or in_weimar_coalition : However, our coalition partners are more supportive of the idea of "shared sacrifice" than simply taxing the rich. ?] Increasing taxes also decreases economic demand, which may lead to more unemployment. [? if in_grand_coalition or in_weimar_coalition: The liberals in our governing coalition will also face backlash from their support base for participating in the government that increases their own taxes. ?]

@regressive
title: Lower taxes on the rich, while increasing consumption taxes (which affect the working class more).
subtitle: This does not change overall revenue. [? if upper_tax_rates < -5 : Rich tax rates are too low to cut anymore. ?] [? if lower_tax_rates > 5 : Lower-class tax rates are too high to increase. ?]
choose-if: lower_tax_rates <= 5 and upper_tax_rates >= -5 and econ_moderation >= 9
on-arrival: urban_linke -= 6; upper_linke += 2*(1-dissent); youth_linke -= 3; east_linke -= 3; upper_greens += 3*(1-dissent) if greens_in_government; upper_spd += 3*(1-dissent) if spd_in_government; urban_greens -= 5 if greens_in_government; urban_spd -= 5 if spd_in_government; greens_relation -= 4; spd_relation -= 4; fdp_relation += 3*(1-dissent); cdu_relation += 3*(1-dissent); econ_moderation += 1; upper_tax_rates -= 1; lower_tax_rates += 1; urban_linke -= 2 if lower_tax_rates >= 2; capital_strike_progress -= 1 if upper_tax_rates < 0; urban_afd += 3; beweli_dissent += 10; oldleft_dissent += 10; emali_dissent += 10; pragmatist_dissent += 5; greens_coalition_dissent += 1; spd_coalition_dissent += 1;

Our regressive taxation policy benefits the rich while hurting the poor and working-class. Our bourgeois coalition partners approve of this orthodox economic course. [? if in_grand_coalition or in_weimar_coalition: Furthermore, the liberals within our governing coalition will benefit from their participation in the government. This will help dispel the notion that they fail to adequately represent the interests of the middle class while in power. ?]

@tariffs
title: Change tariffs instead.

Tariffs, or taxes on international imports, are another way to finance our government.

Historically, <span style="color: #c00000;">socialists</span> have been in favor of free trade and a low-tariff regime. Workers in export-oriented industries benefit from free trade, and they also benefit from lower prices for imported necessities. Do the present economic circumstances change these calculations?

Current tariff level: [+ tariffs : taxation +]

- @raise_tariffs
- @lower_tariffs
- @fiscal_menu: Change domestic taxes instead of tariffs.
- @root: Do not change tariffs or taxes.
- @easy_discard

@raise_tariffs
title: Raise tariffs on imports.
subtitle: +2 budget. Other countries will retaliate by increasing tariffs of their own. [? if tariffs > 5 : Further increases in tariffs will not raise revenue, as we have already nearly reached economic autarky. ?]
choose-if: tariffs <= 5
on-arrival: tariffs += 1; inflation += 1 if inflation > 0; inflation += 0.5 if inflation <= 0; unemployed += 1.5; budget += 2; urban_linke -= 6; east_linke -= 6; youth_linke -= 5; rural_linke += 4*(1-dissent); upper_linke += 3*(1-dissent); greens_relation -= 3; spd_relation -= 1; fdp_relation -= 2; cdu_relation -= 2; usa_relation -= 1; russia_relation -= 1; economic_growth -= 0.4; beweli_dissent += 2; emali_dissent += 2; pragmatist_dissent += 2;

Increasing tariffs leads to higher prices for basic goods, increasing inflation and hurting consumption among the working class. Retaliatory tariffs reduce the competitiveness of German exports, raising unemployment among workers. They also lead to an atmosphere of international suspicion, reducing our ability to negotiate with other countries.

On the other hand, agricultural producers and some small businesses benefit from higher tariffs, as farmers can now command higher prices for grain, and formerly uncompetitive businesses are now able to function.

@lower_tariffs
title: Lower tariffs on imports.
choose-if: budget >= 2 and tariffs > -5
subtitle: -2 budget. [? if tariffs <= -5 : There are no tariffs left to cut. ?]
on-arrival: tariffs -= 1; budget -= 2; inflation -= 0.5; urban_linke += 3*(1-dissent); youth_linke += 3*(1-dissent); east_linke += 3*(1-dissent); rural_linke -= 5; upper_linke -= 3; usa_relation += 1; russia_relation += 1; economic_growth += 0.4;

Lowering tariffs helps workers and the urban poor by reducing prices for basic necessities. In addition, other countries are pleased by lower tariffs, and are more willing to negotiate on many issues.

Farmers are hurt by this policy, as cheap imported grain leads to ruin for some small producers. In general, cheap imports are detrimental for small-scale industries aimed at the domestic market. Those negatively affected have rallied behind the [? if not kvp_formed: <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**DNVP**</span>?][? if kvp_formed: <span style="color: #0087DC;">**KVP**</span>?][? if dnvp_ideology == "Radical":, stoking their urgency to reenter government to act upon this?]. 
